title:: CaosGear
summary:: CaosBox instruments: percussion, basses, pads, chords and lineIn.
categories:: CaosBox
related:: Classes/CaosBox, Classes/CaosInstrument, Classes/CaosTrack

description::
CaosGear builds voices and registers them on the corresponding track. Each method
returns a link::Classes/CaosInstrument::; the track it plays on is chosen with
code::toTrack:: or with the instrument name.

Percussive instruments store the function on each step (snapshot). Melodic
instruments store only the gate and resolve the voice when the step fires (live).

classmethods::

subsection:: Variant registry

method:: waveforms
List of valid waveform symbols for code::pad:::
code::[sin, tri, pulse]::

method:: chordVariants
Dictionary of valid chord sets, keyed by instrument family:
code::\chords:: and code::\chords2::.

method:: validChords
Returns the chord list for one family.
code::
CaosGear.waveforms;                    // [ sin, tri, pulse ]
CaosGear.validChords(\chords);         // M, m, M7, ...
CaosGear.validChords(\chords2);        // M, m, M9, M9m, ...
CaosGear.chordVariants[\chords2];      // same list
::

method:: waveformDef
method:: chordDef
Map a validated symbol to its SynthDef name.
code::
CaosGear.waveformDef('tri');           // \ambuno_tri
CaosGear.chordDef('M7', \chords);      // \acordesuno_M7
CaosGear.chordDef('M9', \chords2);     // \acordesdos_M9
::

instancemethods::

subsection:: Percussion

method:: kick
method:: snare
method:: hihats
method:: kick2
method:: snare2
method:: hihats2
code::
k = CaosGear.new;
k.kick(out: \master);
::

subsection:: Melodic

method:: bass
method:: bass2
method:: pad
method:: pad2
method:: chords
method:: chords2
method:: lineIn

code::
g = CaosGear.new;
g.bass(out: \reverb, semitoneArray: [48, 50, 52, 55]);
g.pad(waveform: 'tri');
g.chords(chordsArray: #['m', 'M']);
::

note:: code::waveform:: and the first element of code::chordsArray:: choose the
SynthDef variant when the instrument is created. To change it later, use
link::Classes/CaosInstrument#-updateTimbre::. code::set(\chord, ...):: does not
change the SynthDef.
::

subsection:: Track routing

method:: toTrack
method:: offTrack
code::
k.toTrack([0, 4, 8, 12]);
k.offTrack;
::
